{%- comment -%}
  The real multi-pack automatic discounts, as data, in one place.

  Pulled from the live Shopify discounts, not from the brief:

    "2-Pack Supplement Discount (25% off)"  min quantity 2
    "3-Pack Supplement Discount (40% off)"  min quantity 3

  Two facts about them that the storefront copy has to respect:

  1. They are QUANTITY tiers, not a subscription offer. Both have
     appliesOnOneTimePurchase AND appliesOnSubscription true, so wording like
     "25% off monthly" is wrong -- monthly delivery is the separate Subscribe
     & Save selling plan, a different mechanism. Say "add a 2nd pack", never
     "monthly".

  2. They are scoped to exactly the 12 product IDs below, NOT the whole
     66-pack catalogue. Six are the live handles; the other six are older
     duplicate products carrying the same titles, kept here so a real match is
     never missed. Anything not on this list must never be shown a hardcoded
     percentage -- that is the same broken-promise failure as the catalogue
     truncation bug fixed earlier in this project.

  Consumed as JSON by both sections/spadra-stack.liquid (the PDP checkbox
  picker) and sections/native-quiz-modal.liquid (the results banner), so the
  two can never drift apart.

  If the discounts change in Shopify admin, re-query discountNodes and edit
  this file only.

  Usage: {% render 'spadra-stack-discounts' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

<script type="application/json" data-spadra-stack-discounts>
  {
    "eligible": [
      "sleep-pack",
      "sleep-pack-1",
      "sleep-pack-2",
      "sleep-pack-3",
      "performance-pack",
      "performance-pack-1",
      "brain-pack-1",
      "muscle-preserve-pack",
      "muscle-preserve-pack-1",
      "muscle-preserve-pack-spadra",
      "focus-pack-spadra",
      "sleep-pack-melatonin-spadra"
    ],
    "tiers": [
      { "qty": 3, "percent": 40 },
      { "qty": 2, "percent": 25 }
    ]
  }
</script>
